# i3 config file (v4)
#
# The v4 marker is load-bearing — see the shared config for why.
#
# No per-side outer gap (docs/adr/0015), and no `smart_borders`: native i3 4.22
# rejects that i3-gaps directive outright and raises i3-nagbar over the top of
# the screenshot — see monolith/i3.config.

font pango:JetBrains Mono 10

# 20, wide on purpose: the heat field is continuous across the whole screen and
# the gap is where you see that the windows are cropping one image rather than
# each painting their own.
gaps inner 20

default_border pixel 2
new_window pixel 2

# Border colour is the one per-window channel i3 offers, and it is not
# per-window: it is per *state*. Focused is peak, unfocused is cool. A window's
# own temperature cannot reach it — see the report, section B.
client.focused          #F4D660 #120F1C #F1E7E2 #F4D660 #F4D660
client.unfocused        #5C3076 #120F1C #9A8FA8 #5C3076 #5C3076
client.focused_inactive #5C3076 #120F1C #9A8FA8 #5C3076 #5C3076
client.urgent           #D6702C #120F1C #F1E7E2 #D6702C #D6702C
